WEBVTT

00:02.467 --> 00:03.885
KATARA: Water.

00:04.761 --> 00:06.137
Earth.

00:06.763 --> 00:08.097
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:10.141
Air.

00:11.184 --> 00:15.146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.396 --> 00:18.608
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.651 --> 00:22.529
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.612 --> 00:23.821
could stop them.

00:23.905 --> 00:26.574
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.367 --> 00:29.827
100 years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.911 --> 00:32.705
the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.956 --> 00:35.083
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.166 --> 00:37.752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.835 --> 00:38.920
AANG: Oof.

00:39.128 --> 00:42.090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

00:58.436 --> 01:02.648
( DRILL WHIRRING )

01:10.698 --> 01:12.325
( STEAM HISSING )

01:13.242 --> 01:15.286
( CREAKING )

01:32.887 --> 01:35.139
( WHIRRING )

01:44.440 --> 01:47.068
This drill is a feat
of scientific ingenuity

01:47.151 --> 01:49.320
and raw destructive power.

01:49.737 --> 01:51.530
Once it tunnels
through the wall,

01:51.656 --> 01:53.866
our troops will
storm their city.

01:53.991 --> 01:56.285
The Earth Kingdom
will finally fall.

01:56.661 --> 02:00.206
And you can claim Ba Sing Se
in the name of your father.

02:00.748 --> 02:02.041
Nothing can stop us.

02:02.792 --> 02:06.212
Hmm, what about those
muscle-y guys down there?

02:08.798 --> 02:10.132
( DRILL WHIRRING )

02:10.216 --> 02:12.385
Please, the drill's metal shell

02:12.468 --> 02:15.012
is impervious to any
earthbending attack.

02:15.304 --> 02:17.974
Oh, I'm sure it is, War Minister Qin.

02:18.057 --> 02:19.642
But just to be
on the safe side,

02:19.934 --> 02:22.895
Mai and Ty Lee,
take the Earthbenders out.

02:22.979 --> 02:25.064
Finally, something to do.

02:30.778 --> 02:32.113
( MOMO CHATTERS )

02:32.488 --> 02:35.866
Aang, what are you doing here?
I thought you were looking for Appa.

02:35.950 --> 02:39.245
I was, but something
stopped me― Something big.

02:46.085 --> 02:48.337
SOKKA: Now, what's so big
that Appa has to wait?

02:49.338 --> 02:50.381
AANG: That.

02:51.007 --> 02:52.925
( DRILL WHIRRING )

02:54.385 --> 02:57.096
We made it to Ba Sing Se
and we're still not safe.

02:57.346 --> 02:58.431
No one is.

02:59.515 --> 03:01.100
What are you people doing here?

03:01.183 --> 03:02.977
Civilians aren't allowed on the wall.

03:03.602 --> 03:06.647
I'm the Avatar.
Take me to whoever's in charge.

03:07.982 --> 03:11.819
It is an honor to welcome you
to the Outer Wall, young Avatar.

03:12.403 --> 03:13.863
But your help is not needed.

03:14.280 --> 03:17.325
- Not needed?
- Not needed.

03:17.616 --> 03:20.244
I have the situation
under control.

03:20.536 --> 03:24.248
I assure you, the Fire Nation
cannot penetrate this wall.

03:25.374 --> 03:29.420
Many have tried to break through it,
but none have succeeded.

03:30.421 --> 03:33.132
What about the Dragon of the West?
He got in.

03:33.215 --> 03:38.721
Well, technically, yes.
But he was quickly expunged.

03:39.680 --> 03:44.143
Nevertheless, that's why the city
is named Ba Sing Se.

03:44.268 --> 03:46.937
It's the impenetrable city.

03:47.063 --> 03:49.398
They don't call it Na Sing Se!

03:49.482 --> 03:53.069
( LAUGHS ) That means penetrable city.

03:53.694 --> 03:54.945
Yeah, thanks for the tour.

03:55.029 --> 03:56.822
But we still got the drill problem.

03:57.239 --> 03:58.616
Not for long.

03:58.699 --> 04:01.952
To stop it, I've sent an elite
platoon of Earthbenders

04:02.036 --> 04:04.246
called the Terra Team.

04:04.330 --> 04:06.791
That's a good group name. Very catchy.

04:10.419 --> 04:11.420
( GRUNTING )

04:11.879 --> 04:13.339
( RUMBLING )

04:14.882 --> 04:17.510
Ready? Attack!

04:23.140 --> 04:24.600
( CREAKING )

04:26.852 --> 04:28.020
( GRUNTING )

04:36.779 --> 04:38.322
( GRUNTS )

04:40.116 --> 04:41.659
( GRUNTS )

04:44.829 --> 04:45.913
( GRUNTING )

04:47.164 --> 04:48.249
( GROANS )

04:49.500 --> 04:51.293
We're doomed!

04:52.169 --> 04:54.088
Get a hold of yourself, man!

04:54.171 --> 04:55.631
You're right. I'm sorry.

04:56.132 --> 04:58.467
Maybe you'd like the Avatar's help now?

05:01.554 --> 05:02.721
( MEEKLY ) Yes, please.

05:05.641 --> 05:08.602
So the question is, how
are we gonna stop that thing?

05:10.729 --> 05:14.024
- Why are you all looking at me?
- You're the idea guy.

05:14.483 --> 05:17.069
So I'm the only one who
could ever come up with a plan?

05:17.153 --> 05:18.696
That's a lot of pressure.

05:18.779 --> 05:21.407
- And also, the complaining guy.
- That part I don't mind.

05:25.619 --> 05:30.249
So, Mr. Lee and Mister, um...
"Mushy," is it?

05:30.583 --> 05:31.834
It's pronounced "Moo-shi."

05:32.835 --> 05:34.753
You telling me how to do my job?

05:34.837 --> 05:36.881
Uh, no, no, no.

05:36.964 --> 05:40.134
But may I just say,
you're like a flower in bloom.

05:40.217 --> 05:43.012
Your beauty's intoxicating.

05:43.721 --> 05:47.057
Mmm, you're pretty easy on
the eyes yourself, handsome.

05:47.141 --> 05:48.392
Rawr!

05:48.809 --> 05:50.352
Welcome to Ba Sing Se.

05:53.772 --> 05:55.483
I'm gonna forget I saw that.

05:59.236 --> 06:01.572
I think Lee would make
a good Freedom Fighter.

06:01.947 --> 06:04.742
He's just trying to find his
way in the world, like us.

06:04.825 --> 06:07.036
You don't know
anything about him, Jet.

06:07.119 --> 06:09.497
I know he didn't get that
scar from a Waterbender.

06:09.580 --> 06:11.916
Besides, I thought we
were going straight now.

06:11.999 --> 06:15.544
We are. And the new Freedom Fighters
could use a guy like Lee.

06:15.628 --> 06:16.962
What do you think, Longshot?

06:19.548 --> 06:20.883
I can respect that.

06:23.219 --> 06:25.804
What's wrong with him?
He doesn't look injured.

06:25.888 --> 06:27.097
His qi is blocked.

06:28.807 --> 06:32.144
- Who did this to you?
- Two girls ambushed us.

06:32.561 --> 06:35.064
One of them hit me with
a bunch of quick jabs.

06:35.147 --> 06:36.899
And suddenly, I couldn't earthbend,

06:36.982 --> 06:40.194
and I could barely move.
And then she cartwheeled away.

06:41.362 --> 06:43.656
Ty Lee. She doesn't look dangerous,

06:43.739 --> 06:46.242
but she knows the human body
and its weak points.

06:46.325 --> 06:48.869
It's like she takes you down
from the inside.

06:49.078 --> 06:51.580
- Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!
- Yes?

06:51.664 --> 06:52.790
What you just said.

06:52.873 --> 06:54.959
That's how we're gonna
take down the drill―

06:55.042 --> 06:57.711
The same way Ty Lee took
down all these big Earthbenders.

06:57.795 --> 06:59.630
By hitting its pressure points!

07:01.966 --> 07:03.968
We'll take it down from the inside.

07:08.180 --> 07:11.809
( DRILL WHIRRING )

07:12.434 --> 07:15.312
Once I whip up some cover,
you're not gonna be able to see,

07:15.396 --> 07:16.689
so stay close to me.

07:17.940 --> 07:20.234
( RUMBLING )

07:25.155 --> 07:26.407
TOPH: Run!

07:26.532 --> 07:27.575
( MOMO CHATTERS )

07:29.076 --> 07:31.412
Hey, look at that dust cloud.

07:31.537 --> 07:35.374
It's so... Poofy. Poof!

07:36.166 --> 07:38.836
Don't worry, Princess.
I'm sure it's nothing.

07:40.504 --> 07:41.922
( DRILL WHIRRING )

07:47.678 --> 07:49.722
( RUMBLING )

07:49.847 --> 07:51.181
Everyone into the hole.

07:55.603 --> 07:58.272
SOKKA: It's so dark down here.
I can't see a thing.

07:58.355 --> 08:00.691
TOPH: ( SARCASTICALLY )
Oh, no, what a nightmare!

08:00.816 --> 08:01.900
SOKKA: Sorry.

08:02.026 --> 08:04.612
( DRILL WHIRRING )

08:07.448 --> 08:08.741
There.

08:08.824 --> 08:09.825
( MOMO CHATTERS )

08:10.909 --> 08:11.910
( GRUNTS )

08:12.953 --> 08:13.954
( GRUNTS )

08:16.081 --> 08:17.291
Toph, come on!

08:17.416 --> 08:19.376
No way am I going in that metal monster.

08:19.501 --> 08:20.753
I can't bend in there.

08:20.878 --> 08:22.630
I'll try to slow it down out here.

08:22.755 --> 08:24.298
Okay, good luck.

08:26.342 --> 08:27.551
( RUMBLING )

08:28.177 --> 08:30.137
( GRUNTS )

08:33.974 --> 08:36.143
I need a plan of this machine,
some schematics

08:36.226 --> 08:38.020
that show what the inside looks like.

08:38.103 --> 08:39.730
Then we can find
its weak points.

08:39.813 --> 08:41.857
Where are we gonna
get something like that?

08:41.940 --> 08:42.983
( CLANG )

08:43.067 --> 08:45.486
What are you doing?
Someone's gonna hear us.

08:45.694 --> 08:46.820
That's the point.

08:46.904 --> 08:49.782
I figure a machine this big
needs engineers to run it.

08:49.865 --> 08:52.701
- And when something breaks...
- They come to fix it.

08:52.785 --> 08:53.786
( GAS HISSING )

08:59.792 --> 09:00.793
Hi.

09:02.461 --> 09:03.962
This'll work, thanks!

09:04.588 --> 09:05.589
( CLANGS )

09:09.885 --> 09:12.638
It looks like the drill
is made up of two main structures.

09:12.721 --> 09:15.891
There's the inner mechanism,
where we are now, and the outer shell.

09:15.974 --> 09:18.977
The inner part and the outer part
are connected by these braces.

09:19.061 --> 09:21.689
If we cut through them, the
entire thing will collapse.

09:26.360 --> 09:29.029
So, you guys got plans
once you're inside the city?

09:29.113 --> 09:32.741
MAN: Get your hot tea here!
Finest tea in Ba Sing Se!

09:33.158 --> 09:35.202
Oh, Jasmine, please!

09:40.374 --> 09:42.751
( COUGHS )

09:43.419 --> 09:46.338
Coldest tea in Ba Sing Se
is more like it.

09:46.463 --> 09:48.257
What a disgrace!

09:48.382 --> 09:50.134
Hey, can I talk to you for a second?

09:52.219 --> 09:53.804
( SIGHS )

09:53.929 --> 09:56.807
You and I have a much better
chance of making it in the city

09:56.890 --> 09:58.225
if we stick together.

09:58.350 --> 10:00.561
You wanna join the Freedom Fighters?

10:00.686 --> 10:03.564
Thanks, but I don't think
you want me in your gang.

10:03.647 --> 10:06.400
Come on, we made a great team
looting that captain's food.

10:06.483 --> 10:08.986
Think of all the good we
could do for these refugees.

10:09.069 --> 10:10.154
I said no.

10:11.280 --> 10:12.364
Have it your way.

10:13.282 --> 10:14.783
( SLURPS )

10:23.584 --> 10:24.626
Hey!

10:24.710 --> 10:27.004
What are you doing firebending your tea?

10:27.087 --> 10:30.090
For a wise old man, that
was a pretty stupid move.

10:30.174 --> 10:33.677
I know you're not supposed
to cry over spilled tea, but...

10:33.761 --> 10:37.723
-( SNIFFLES ) It's just so sad!
-( TRAGIC VIOLIN PLAYS )

10:37.973 --> 10:40.601
( DRILL WHIRRING )

10:41.810 --> 10:44.855
Wow, it looks a lot thicker in person
than it does in the plans.

10:44.938 --> 10:47.608
We're gonna have to work pretty
hard to cut through that.

10:47.691 --> 10:49.151
What's this "we" stuff?

10:49.234 --> 10:51.361
Aang and I are gonna
have to do all the work.

10:51.445 --> 10:53.197
Look, I'm the plan guy.

10:53.280 --> 10:55.824
You two are the cut stuff
up with waterbending guys.

10:55.908 --> 10:57.951
Together, we're Team Avatar.

11:00.412 --> 11:05.584
( METAL SLICING )

11:13.926 --> 11:15.636
( PANTING )

11:15.719 --> 11:17.304
Come on, team! Don't quit now!

11:17.387 --> 11:19.139
- We're―
-( GROWLS )

11:19.223 --> 11:21.600
I mean, you're almost there!

11:23.227 --> 11:27.815
( METAL SLICING )

11:27.940 --> 11:28.941
( MOMO CHATTERS )

11:30.859 --> 11:32.236
( CREAKING )

11:34.822 --> 11:36.156
( SIGHS )

11:36.240 --> 11:39.743
At this rate, we won't do enough damage
before the drill reaches the wall.

11:39.827 --> 11:42.871
I don't know how many
more of those I have in me.

11:43.288 --> 11:45.040
( CREAKING )

11:45.123 --> 11:47.584
( RUMBLING )

11:48.252 --> 11:50.629
Do you hear that? We took it down!

11:50.712 --> 11:52.339
We better get out of here fast.

11:54.299 --> 11:56.385
QIN ( ON PA ):
Congratulations, crew!

11:56.510 --> 11:59.847
The drill has made contact
with the wall of Ba Sing Se.

11:59.972 --> 12:02.558
Start the countdown to victory!

12:02.683 --> 12:06.937
( CREW CHEERING )

12:09.565 --> 12:11.066
( DRILL WHIRRING )

12:20.284 --> 12:21.618
( DRILL WHIRRING )

12:29.376 --> 12:30.627
( GRUNTS )

12:30.711 --> 12:32.671
Come on, brace! Budge!

12:34.131 --> 12:36.800
( GRUNTS )

12:37.092 --> 12:39.428
This is bad. Really bad.

12:40.012 --> 12:43.348
( PANTING ) We're putting everything
we've got into busting these braces,

12:43.432 --> 12:44.683
but it's taking too long!

12:46.059 --> 12:48.270
Maybe we don't need to
cut all the way through.

12:48.729 --> 12:49.938
Toph has been teaching me

12:50.022 --> 12:53.400
that you shouldn't give 100%
of your energy into any one strike.

12:53.692 --> 12:55.611
Sokka, take a fighting stance.

12:55.694 --> 12:58.113
You've gotta be quick and accurate.

12:58.196 --> 13:01.450
Hit a series of points
and break your opponent's stance.

13:01.533 --> 13:04.703
And when he's reeling back,
you deliver the final blow.

13:04.786 --> 13:07.372
His own weight becomes
his downfall, literally.

13:08.123 --> 13:12.002
So we just need to weaken the braces
instead of cutting all the way through.

13:12.085 --> 13:13.879
Then I'll go to the top of this thing

13:13.962 --> 13:15.380
and deliver the final blow.

13:15.464 --> 13:18.091
And boom, it all comes crashing down!

13:18.342 --> 13:23.639
Everyone inside that wall,
the whole world, is counting on us.

13:23.722 --> 13:25.933
The whole world minus
the Fire Nation, that is.

13:27.851 --> 13:29.394
( GRUNTS )

13:29.478 --> 13:32.814
Come on, Twinkle Toes! Hurry up!

13:33.857 --> 13:39.696
( METAL SLICING )

13:45.702 --> 13:47.871
That's enough!
We need to get to the next one.

13:55.087 --> 13:57.547
MAN ( ON PA ): War Minister!
An engineer was ambushed.

13:57.631 --> 13:59.257
His schematics were stolen.

13:59.341 --> 14:00.592
MAN ( ON PA ): War Minister!

14:00.676 --> 14:03.345
A brace on the starboard side
has been cut clean through!

14:03.428 --> 14:04.805
It's sabotage, sir!

14:06.348 --> 14:07.557
Let's go, ladies.

14:09.226 --> 14:10.560
-( SPLASHING )
-( METAL SLICING )

14:10.644 --> 14:12.062
Good work, Team Avatar.

14:12.145 --> 14:14.231
Now Aang just needs to― Duck!

14:16.233 --> 14:17.234
Whoa!

14:17.943 --> 14:21.363
Wow, Azula, you were right!
It is the Avatar...

14:21.655 --> 14:22.948
...and friends.

14:23.949 --> 14:24.950
Hey.

14:25.867 --> 14:26.868
Aah!

14:29.454 --> 14:30.455
Whoa!

14:32.165 --> 14:33.250
( MOMO CHATTERS )

14:35.419 --> 14:38.255
Guys, get out of here!
I know what I need to do.

14:38.338 --> 14:40.716
Wait, you need this water
more than I do.

14:47.055 --> 14:48.807
Follow them. The Avatar's mine.

14:53.270 --> 14:54.646
Slurry pipeline?

14:54.730 --> 14:56.189
-( GRUNTS )
- What does that mean?

14:56.273 --> 14:57.691
( GRUNTS )

14:58.900 --> 15:00.569
It's rock and water mixed together.

15:00.652 --> 15:02.070
It means our way out.

15:04.197 --> 15:05.907
-( PANTING )
-( SPLASHES )

15:07.617 --> 15:08.827
( SCREAMING )

15:10.787 --> 15:13.206
Ugh, disgusting.

15:13.290 --> 15:16.710
Come on, you heard Azula.
We have to follow them.

15:16.793 --> 15:19.212
She can shoot all the
lightning she wants at me.

15:19.296 --> 15:22.132
I am not going in that
wall sludge juice.

15:22.215 --> 15:23.300
( SIGHS )

15:25.552 --> 15:26.803
( SPLASHES )

15:27.262 --> 15:28.263
Ugh.

15:39.483 --> 15:42.402
( SOKKA AND KATARA SCREAMING )

15:44.821 --> 15:45.822
Ugh!

15:45.906 --> 15:50.035
( GROANS AND WHINES )

15:50.118 --> 15:51.328
( MOANS )

15:57.042 --> 15:58.710
( SCREAMS )

16:00.045 --> 16:01.338
( WHIMPERS )

16:01.421 --> 16:04.549
Why don't you try blocking
my qi now, circus freak?

16:04.633 --> 16:06.051
Katara, keep that up.

16:06.134 --> 16:08.011
The pressure will
build up in the drill.

16:08.095 --> 16:11.139
Then, when Aang delivers the final blow,
it'll be ready to pop!

16:11.223 --> 16:12.682
( RUMBLING )

16:14.142 --> 16:17.062
( MOMO CHATTERS )

16:19.773 --> 16:21.566
This looks like a good spot, Momo.

16:22.442 --> 16:23.944
( EXCLAIMS )

16:27.239 --> 16:31.660
General Sung, tell your soldiers
to stop shooting rocks down here!

16:32.285 --> 16:33.912
Soldiers, whatever you do,

16:33.995 --> 16:36.123
don't stop shooting rocks down there!

16:39.793 --> 16:42.087
( CRASHING )

16:43.380 --> 16:45.048
( METAL SLICING )

16:51.263 --> 16:54.349
Good technique, Little Sister.
Keep it up!

16:54.432 --> 16:56.059
Don't forget to breathe.

16:56.143 --> 17:00.063
You know, I am just about sick and tired
of you telling me what to do all day.

17:00.147 --> 17:01.940
You're like a chattering hog monkey.

17:02.023 --> 17:03.775
Just bend the slurry, woman!

17:04.401 --> 17:06.486
-( SCREAMS )
- TOPH: You guys need some help?

17:06.570 --> 17:08.530
Toph, help me plug up this drain.

17:15.120 --> 17:16.663
( CREAKING )

17:19.624 --> 17:22.127
( METAL SLICING )

17:23.211 --> 17:24.588
( PANTING )

17:24.671 --> 17:26.423
What I'd give
to be a Metalbender.

17:26.506 --> 17:27.632
( SQUEALS )

17:30.260 --> 17:32.304
- Momo, get out of here!
-( CHATTERS )

17:47.027 --> 17:48.570
( WATER SPLASHING )

17:57.746 --> 17:59.831
- Aah!
-( CRASHING )

18:04.336 --> 18:05.337
( GASPS )

18:11.301 --> 18:13.970
( GRUNTS )

18:15.931 --> 18:16.932
( GRUNTS )

18:21.478 --> 18:22.520
( GRUNTS )

18:28.735 --> 18:29.736
( GRUNTS )

18:30.362 --> 18:31.821
( GAS HISSING )

18:32.864 --> 18:34.241
( CREAKING )

18:35.533 --> 18:37.827
( RUMBLING )

18:48.088 --> 18:49.923
( WHIMPERS )

18:56.263 --> 18:57.347
( GRUNTS )

19:07.524 --> 19:08.525
Whoa!

19:13.571 --> 19:14.572
Aah!

19:17.075 --> 19:18.243
( GRUNTS )

19:31.047 --> 19:33.717
-( CHATTERS )
-( GRUNTS )

19:39.014 --> 19:40.932
Thanks, Momo. I owe you one.

19:46.313 --> 19:48.481
- Now all I need is a―
-( CRASHES )

19:48.565 --> 19:50.567
Actually, that is what I needed, for once.

19:50.650 --> 19:51.776
( MOMO CHATTERS )

19:54.529 --> 19:57.615
( STONE CRACKING )

20:17.427 --> 20:19.179
Aah!

20:31.358 --> 20:32.359
Aah!

20:36.154 --> 20:37.405
Aah!

20:38.615 --> 20:39.783
( CREAKING )

20:40.784 --> 20:42.077
( CREAKING )

20:46.498 --> 20:49.626
( SPLASHING )

20:49.709 --> 20:51.252
- Woo-hoo!
- Here it comes!

20:56.424 --> 20:57.425
Whoa!

21:03.681 --> 21:05.308
( CREAKING )

21:08.978 --> 21:11.147
( DRILL POWERS DOWN )

21:19.030 --> 21:20.323
( CHATTERS )

21:34.254 --> 21:36.005
( SPUTTERS ) Ugh!

21:44.097 --> 21:45.306
We lost.

21:46.766 --> 21:49.185
MAN: Last call for Ba Sing Se!

21:49.561 --> 21:51.312
Jet, relax.

21:51.396 --> 21:53.982
So the old guy had some hot tea. Big deal!

21:54.065 --> 21:58.236
He heated it himself.
Those guys are Firebenders.

22:09.414 --> 22:12.834
- What a handsome baby.
- Thank you.

22:33.521 --> 22:36.774
SOKKA: I just wanted to say
good effort out there today, Team Avatar.

22:36.858 --> 22:39.360
Enough with the Team Avatar stuff.

22:39.444 --> 22:42.322
No matter how many times you
say it, it's not gonna catch on.

22:42.405 --> 22:45.575
How about the Boomerang Squad?

22:45.658 --> 22:47.660
See, it's good 'cause
it's got "ang" in it.

22:47.744 --> 22:49.370
Boomer-Aang!

22:49.454 --> 22:50.788
I kinda like that one.

22:50.872 --> 22:53.249
Let's talk about this
on our way into the city.

22:53.333 --> 22:55.376
- The Aang Gang?
- KATARA: Sokka...

22:55.460 --> 22:57.795
- The Fearsome Foursome!
- TOPH: You're crazy.

22:57.879 --> 22:59.255
Why? We're fearsome!
